        "message": "Setting boundaries while sharing a living space works best when your response is short, consistent, and doesn’t invite a debate. A few ways to handle it: * **A standard script:** Pick one neutral phrase and stick to it every time it comes up, without overexplaining. Something like: *“I prefer to keep that part of my life private. If there’s ever news I want to share, I will.”*\n* **Answer and pivot:** Give a flat, final answer and immediately change the subject to something everyday: *“No updates there. Did anyone figure out dinner tonight?”*\n* **A neutral exit:** If they keep pressing, remove yourself without making it a confrontation: *“I’m going to head to my room to unwind for a bit.”* Having a pre-planned line ready takes the pressure off deciding how to react in the moment, and repeating the same response gives them very little to push back against.",
